# Computationally intensive code

When implementing computationally intensive operations, check:

- Can the implementation be sped up by reusing computations already done by other iterations? (Whether because a computation is shared by multiple iterations or there is a dynamic programming approach)
- Can the implementation be sped up by vectorizing it?

# Jupyter / imports

The IPython notebook kernel keeps stale modules and old class instances.

- Use a module to reload modules in dependency order.
- Make sure the notebook recreates existing instances, which are not updated by reloading modules.
